{"route":"/docs/5.3/utilities/background/","version":"5.3","renderedVersion":"5.3","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Background","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Convey meaning through <code>background-color</code> and add decoration with gradients."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"content--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Accessibility tip:</strong> Using color to add meaning only provides a visual indication, which will not be conveyed to users of assistive technologies like screen readers. Please ensure the meaning is obvious from the content itself (e.g., the visible text with a <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/accessibility/#color-contrast\"><em>sufficient</em> color contrast</a>) or is included through alternative means, such as additional text hidden with the <code>.visually-hidden</code> class."}]},{"id":"background-color","type":"heading","en":"Background color","level":2},{"id":"background-color--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Similar to the contextual text color classes, set the background of an element to any contextual class. Background utilities <strong>do not set <code>color</code></strong>, so in some cases you’ll want to use <code>.text-*</code> <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/colors\">color utilities</a>."},{"id":"background-color--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"background-color--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Background utilities like <code>.bg-*</code> that generated from our original <code>$theme-colors</code> Sass map don’t yet respond to color modes, however, any <code>.bg-*-subtle</code> utility will. This will be resolved in v6."}]},{"id":"background-color--example-1","type":"demo","key":"96b16600a8cc43a5e79e","height":300},{"id":"background-color--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-primary text-white\">.bg-primary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-primary-subtle text-primary-emphasis\">.bg-primary-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-secondary text-white\">.bg-secondary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-secondary-subtle text-secondary-emphasis\">.bg-secondary-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-success text-white\">.bg-success</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-success-subtle text-success-emphasis\">.bg-success-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-danger text-white\">.bg-danger</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-danger-subtle text-danger-emphasis\">.bg-danger-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-warning text-dark\">.bg-warning</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis\">.bg-warning-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-info text-dark\">.bg-info</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-info-subtle text-info-emphasis\">.bg-info-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-light text-dark\">.bg-light</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-light-subtle text-light-emphasis\">.bg-light-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-dark text-white\">.bg-dark</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-dark-subtle text-dark-emphasis\">.bg-dark-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body-secondary\">.bg-body-secondary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body-tertiary\">.bg-body-tertiary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body text-body\">.bg-body</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-black text-white\">.bg-black</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-white text-dark\">.bg-white</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-transparent text-body\">.bg-transparent</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"background-gradient","type":"heading","en":"Background gradient","level":2},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"By adding a <code>.bg-gradient</code> class, a linear gradient is added as background image to the backgrounds. This gradient starts with a semi-transparent white which fades out to the bottom."},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Do you need a gradient in your custom CSS? Just add <code>background-image: var(--bs-gradient);</code>."},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-primary.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-secondary.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-success.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-danger.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-warning.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-info.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-light.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-dark.bg-gradient"},{"id":"background-gradient--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":".bg-black.bg-gradient"},{"id":"opacity","type":"heading","en":"Opacity","level":2},{"id":"opacity--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<small>Added in v5.1.0</small>"},{"id":"opacity--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"As of v5.1.0, <code>background-color</code> utilities are generated with Sass using CSS variables. This allows for real-time color changes without compilation and dynamic alpha transparency changes."},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","en":"How it works","level":3},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Consider our default <code>.bg-success</code> utility."},{"id":"how-it-works--code-1","type":"code","value":".bg-success {\n  --bs-bg-opacity: 1;\n  background-color: rgba(var(--bs-success-rgb), var(--bs-bg-opacity)) !important;\n}","language":"css"},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"We use an RGB version of our <code>--bs-success</code> (with the value of <code>25, 135, 84</code>) CSS variable and attached a second CSS variable, <code>--bs-bg-opacity</code>, for the alpha transparency (with a default value <code>1</code> thanks to a local CSS variable). That means anytime you use <code>.bg-success</code> now, your computed <code>color</code> value is <code>rgba(25, 135, 84, 1)</code>. The local CSS variable inside each <code>.bg-*</code> class avoids inheritance issues so nested instances of the utilities don’t automatically have a modified alpha transparency."},{"id":"example","type":"heading","en":"Example","level":3},{"id":"example--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"To change that opacity, override <code>--bs-bg-opacity</code> via custom styles or inline styles."},{"id":"example--example-1","type":"demo","key":"2cf0041d74e2f91536d2","height":174},{"id":"example--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white\">This is default success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2\" style=\"--bs-bg-opacity: .5;\">This is 50% opacity success background</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"example--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Or, choose from any of the <code>.bg-opacity</code> utilities:"},{"id":"example--example-2","type":"demo","key":"636b57f0954d883e1e33","height":300},{"id":"example--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white\">This is default success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white bg-opacity-75\">This is 75% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-50\">This is 50% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-25\">This is 25% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-10\">This is 10% opacity success background</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"css--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"In addition to the following Sass functionality, consider reading about our included <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/customize/css-variables\">CSS custom properties</a> (aka CSS variables) for colors and more."},{"id":"sass-variables","type":"heading","en":"Sass variables","level":3},{"id":"sass-variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Most <code>background-color</code> utilities are generated by our theme colors, reassigned from our generic color palette variables."},{"id":"sass-variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"$blue:    #0d6efd;\n$indigo:  #6610f2;\n$purple:  #6f42c1;\n$pink:    #d63384;\n$red:     #dc3545;\n$orange:  #fd7e14;\n$yellow:  #ffc107;\n$green:   #198754;\n$teal:    #20c997;\n$cyan:    #0dcaf0;","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-variables--code-2","type":"code","value":"$primary:       $blue;\n$secondary:     $gray-600;\n$success:       $green;\n$info:          $cyan;\n$warning:       $yellow;\n$danger:        $red;\n$light:         $gray-100;\n$dark:          $gray-900;","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-variables--code-3","type":"code","value":"$gradient: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba($white, .15), rgba($white, 0));","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-variables--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Grayscale colors are also available, but only a subset are used to generate any utilities."},{"id":"sass-variables--code-4","type":"code","value":"$white:    #fff;\n$gray-100: #f8f9fa;\n$gray-200: #e9ecef;\n$gray-300: #dee2e6;\n$gray-400: #ced4da;\n$gray-500: #adb5bd;\n$gray-600: #6c757d;\n$gray-700: #495057;\n$gray-800: #343a40;\n$gray-900: #212529;\n$black:    #000;","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-variables--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Variables for setting <code>background-color</code> in <code>.bg-*-subtle</code> utilities in light and dark mode:"},{"id":"sass-variables--code-5","type":"code","value":"$primary-bg-subtle:       tint-color($primary, 80%);\n$secondary-bg-subtle:     tint-color($secondary, 80%);\n$success-bg-subtle:       tint-color($success, 80%);\n$info-bg-subtle:          tint-color($info, 80%);\n$warning-bg-subtle:       tint-color($warning, 80%);\n$danger-bg-subtle:        tint-color($danger, 80%);\n$light-bg-subtle:         mix($gray-100, $white);\n$dark-bg-subtle:          $gray-400;","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-variables--code-6","type":"code","value":"$primary-bg-subtle-dark:            shade-color($primary, 80%);\n$secondary-bg-subtle-dark:          shade-color($secondary, 80%);\n$success-bg-subtle-dark:            shade-color($success, 80%);\n$info-bg-subtle-dark:               shade-color($info, 80%);\n$warning-bg-subtle-dark:            shade-color($warning, 80%);\n$danger-bg-subtle-dark:             shade-color($danger, 80%);\n$light-bg-subtle-dark:              $gray-800;\n$dark-bg-subtle-dark:               mix($gray-800, $black);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps","type":"heading","en":"Sass maps","level":3},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Theme colors are then put into a Sass map so we can loop over them to generate our utilities, component modifiers, and more."},{"id":"sass-maps--code-1","type":"code","value":"$theme-colors: (\n  \"primary\":    $primary,\n  \"secondary\":  $secondary,\n  \"success\":    $success,\n  \"info\":       $info,\n  \"warning\":    $warning,\n  \"danger\":     $danger,\n  \"light\":      $light,\n  \"dark\":       $dark\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Grayscale colors are also available as a Sass map. <strong>This map is not used to generate any utilities.</strong>"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-2","type":"code","value":"$grays: (\n  \"100\": $gray-100,\n  \"200\": $gray-200,\n  \"300\": $gray-300,\n  \"400\": $gray-400,\n  \"500\": $gray-500,\n  \"600\": $gray-600,\n  \"700\": $gray-700,\n  \"800\": $gray-800,\n  \"900\": $gray-900\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"RGB colors are generated from a separate Sass map:"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-3","type":"code","value":"$theme-colors-rgb: map-loop($theme-colors, to-rgb, \"$value\");","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Background color opacities build on that with their own map that’s consumed by the utilities API:"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-4","type":"code","value":"$utilities-bg: map-merge(\n  $utilities-colors,\n  (\n    \"black\": to-rgb($black),\n    \"white\": to-rgb($white),\n    \"body\": to-rgb($body-bg)\n  )\n);\n$utilities-bg-colors: map-loop($utilities-bg, rgba-css-var, \"$key\", \"bg\");\n\n$utilities-bg-subtle: (\n  \"primary-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}primary-bg-subtle),\n  \"secondary-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}secondary-bg-subtle),\n  \"success-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}success-bg-subtle),\n  \"info-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}info-bg-subtle),\n  \"warning-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}warning-bg-subtle),\n  \"danger-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}danger-bg-subtle),\n  \"light-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}light-bg-subtle),\n  \"dark-subtle\": var(--#{$prefix}dark-bg-subtle)\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Color mode background colors are also available as a Sass map:"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-5","type":"code","value":"$theme-colors-bg-subtle: (\n  \"primary\": $primary-bg-subtle,\n  \"secondary\": $secondary-bg-subtle,\n  \"success\": $success-bg-subtle,\n  \"info\": $info-bg-subtle,\n  \"warning\": $warning-bg-subtle,\n  \"danger\": $danger-bg-subtle,\n  \"light\": $light-bg-subtle,\n  \"dark\": $dark-bg-subtle,\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-6","type":"code","value":"$theme-colors-bg-subtle-dark: (\n  \"primary\": $primary-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"secondary\": $secondary-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"success\": $success-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"info\": $info-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"warning\": $warning-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"danger\": $danger-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"light\": $light-bg-subtle-dark,\n  \"dark\": $dark-bg-subtle-dark,\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-mixins","type":"heading","en":"Sass mixins","level":3},{"id":"sass-mixins--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>No mixins are used to generate our background utilities</strong>, but we do have some additional mixins for other situations where you’d like to create your own gradients."},{"id":"sass-mixins--code-1","type":"code","value":"@mixin gradient-bg($color: null) {\n  background-color: $color;\n\n  @if $enable-gradients {\n    background-image: var(--#{$prefix}gradient);\n  }\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-mixins--code-2","type":"code","value":"// Horizontal gradient, from left to right\n//\n// Creates two color stops, start and end, by specifying a color and position for each color stop.\n@mixin gradient-x($start-color: $gray-700, $end-color: $gray-800, $start-percent: 0%, $end-percent: 100%) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient(to right, $start-color $start-percent, $end-color $end-percent);\n}\n\n// Vertical gradient, from top to bottom\n//\n// Creates two color stops, start and end, by specifying a color and position for each color stop.\n@mixin gradient-y($start-color: $gray-700, $end-color: $gray-800, $start-percent: null, $end-percent: null) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, $start-color $start-percent, $end-color $end-percent);\n}\n\n@mixin gradient-directional($start-color: $gray-700, $end-color: $gray-800, $deg: 45deg) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient($deg, $start-color, $end-color);\n}\n\n@mixin gradient-x-three-colors($start-color: $blue, $mid-color: $purple, $color-stop: 50%, $end-color: $red) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient(to right, $start-color, $mid-color $color-stop, $end-color);\n}\n\n@mixin gradient-y-three-colors($start-color: $blue, $mid-color: $purple, $color-stop: 50%, $end-color: $red) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient($start-color, $mid-color $color-stop, $end-color);\n}\n\n@mixin gradient-radial($inner-color: $gray-700, $outer-color: $gray-800) {\n  background-image: radial-gradient(circle, $inner-color, $outer-color);\n}\n\n@mixin gradient-striped($color: rgba($white, .15), $angle: 45deg) {\n  background-image: linear-gradient($angle, $color 25%, transparent 25%, transparent 50%, $color 50%, $color 75%, transparent 75%, transparent);\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"sass-utilities-api","type":"heading","en":"Sass utilities API","level":3},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Background utilities are declared in our utilities API in <code>scss/_utilities.scss</code>. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/api#using-the-api\">Learn how to use the utilities API.</a>"},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--code-1","type":"code","value":"\"background-color\": (\n  property: background-color,\n  class: bg,\n  local-vars: (\n    \"bg-opacity\": 1\n  ),\n  values: map-merge(\n    $utilities-bg-colors,\n    (\n      \"transparent\": transparent,\n      \"body-secondary\": rgba(var(--#{$prefix}secondary-bg-rgb), var(--#{$prefix}bg-opacity)),\n      \"body-tertiary\": rgba(var(--#{$prefix}tertiary-bg-rgb), var(--#{$prefix}bg-opacity)),\n    )\n  )\n),\n\"bg-opacity\": (\n  css-var: true,\n  class: bg-opacity,\n  values: (\n    10: .1,\n    25: .25,\n    50: .5,\n    75: .75,\n    100: 1\n  )\n),\n\"subtle-background-color\": (\n  property: background-color,\n  class: bg,\n  values: $utilities-bg-subtle\n),","language":"scss"}],"demos":[{"key":"96b16600a8cc43a5e79e","html":" <div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-primary text-white\">.bg-primary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-primary-subtle text-primary-emphasis\">.bg-primary-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-secondary text-white\">.bg-secondary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-secondary-subtle text-secondary-emphasis\">.bg-secondary-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-success text-white\">.bg-success</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-success-subtle text-success-emphasis\">.bg-success-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-danger text-white\">.bg-danger</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-danger-subtle text-danger-emphasis\">.bg-danger-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-warning text-dark\">.bg-warning</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis\">.bg-warning-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-info text-dark\">.bg-info</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-info-subtle text-info-emphasis\">.bg-info-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-light text-dark\">.bg-light</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-light-subtle text-light-emphasis\">.bg-light-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-dark text-white\">.bg-dark</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-dark-subtle text-dark-emphasis\">.bg-dark-subtle</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body-secondary\">.bg-body-secondary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body-tertiary\">.bg-body-tertiary</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-body text-body\">.bg-body</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-black text-white\">.bg-black</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-white text-dark\">.bg-white</div>\n<div class=\"p-3 mb-2 bg-transparent text-body\">.bg-transparent</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0"},"sprite":""},{"key":"2cf0041d74e2f91536d2","html":" <div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white\">This is default success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2\" style=\"--bs-bg-opacity: .5;\">This is 50% opacity success background</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0"},"sprite":""},{"key":"636b57f0954d883e1e33","html":" <div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white\">This is default success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-white bg-opacity-75\">This is 75% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-50\">This is 50% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-25\">This is 25% opacity success background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-success p-2 text-dark bg-opacity-10\">This is 10% opacity success background</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/introduction"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/download"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contents"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstra